*/target/
*/crashes/
.fuzz-cache/

# Re-include lockfiles, which ../.gitignore drops via a blanket `Cargo.lock`
# under its generic "# Rust" section.
#
# That blanket rule is right for programs/* — they are libraries built through
# Anchor, and their versions are pinned by Cargo.toml. It is wrong here. Every
# harness depends on three crucible crates by `branch = "main"`, which carries
# NO version constraint at all: without a committed lock, an upstream push
# silently changes what the fuzzers are built against, and a crash that does or
# does not reproduce can no longer be attributed to our code.
#
# All ten harnesses currently pin crucible at 812cd554.
!Cargo.lock
